analysis_json.math_expression:
Given dst points to a 16x16 block with row stride 'stride' (in bytes) and pixel bit depth bd (8/9/10/12/14). Let P be pixel type: uint8 if bd<=8 else uint16 (stored via uint8_t* buffer). Let top[x]=P(dst[-stride + x]) for x=0..15 and left[y]=P(dst[y*stride - 1]) for y=0..15.

Mode VERT: for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = top[x].
Mode HOR:  for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = left[y].
Mode DC:   dc = (sum_{x=0..15} top[x] + sum_{y=0..15} left[y] + 16) >> 5; for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = dc.
Mode TOP_DC:  dc = (sum_{x=0..15} top[x] + 8) >> 4;  for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = dc.
Mode LEFT_DC: dc = (sum_{y=0..15} left[y] + 8) >> 4; for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = dc.
Mode 128_DC:  v = 1<<(bd-1); for y=0..15, for x=0..15: P(dst[y*stride + x]) = v.
Mode PLANE (H.264 plane):
  H = sum_{i=1..8} i * (top[7+i] - top[7-i]);
  V = sum_{i=1..8} i * (left[7+i] - left[7-i]);
  a = 16 * (top[15] + left[15]);
  b = (5*H + 32) >> 6;
  c = (5*V + 32) >> 6;
  for y=0..15, for x=0..15:
    val = (a + b*(x-7) + c*(y-7) + 16) >> 5;
    P(dst[y*stride + x]) = clip(val, 0, (1<<bd)-1).
